cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "er_epr_lean: Machine-checked finite-dimensional pieces around the ER=EPR conjecture in Lean 4"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 + mathlib library that proves, in finite dimensions, the pieces on each side
  of the ER=EPR conjecture and leaves the conjecture itself as an explicit gap. On the
  EPR side: no-signalling, thermofield-double states, von Neumann entropy facts, a full
  Landauer bound, monogamy for pure marginals, entanglement swapping, and an area law for
  tensor networks. On the ER side: Kruskal non-traversability, beta = 8 pi M from the
  cone-angle condition, and the Unruh/Bogoliubov thermal ratio. In the middle: a no-go
  theorem showing that no fixed finite-dimensional Hamiltonian has Gibbs entropy equal to
  beta^2/(16 pi) on an interval of beta (and that this hinges on the Hamiltonian being
  fixed), an idealized pure-state AMPS contradiction, and a proof that graph-realizable
  entropies form a strict subset of quantum entropies. Most items are textbook
  finite-dimensional facts; the library is not a proof or refutation of ER=EPR. All 599
  theorems depend only on the standard axioms (propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound),
  with 95 reverse drills and 91 machine-checked coupling assertions.
